## How this project is driven

This project runs on [cckit](https://cckit.dev). Every operation is a `cckit` verb you run in the
shell — read state with `cckit sync --llm` before acting, and append `--llm` to any verb for
machine-readable output. `cckit init` registers hooks in `.codex/hooks.json`: a guard that blocks a
commit to the base branch, a guard that blocks raw `gh`/`git` operations a `cckit` verb owns, session
mail (`cckit msg`), and two session-start checks. Codex runs them only after they are trusted
(`/hooks`), and a hook is fast feedback, not enforcement — the rules below apply whether or not one
fires.
<!-- IF:MEMORY -->
Memory hooks are not installed for Codex: they read Claude Code transcripts. If a MemPalace MCP
server is configured, call its tools explicitly (wing `{{WING}}`).
<!-- /IF:MEMORY -->

## Agents

`cckit init` installs one Codex custom agent per role in `.codex/agents/<role>.toml`, rendered from
the same role source as the Claude Code agents. Ask Codex to spawn the matching agent for a domain
task. A Claude tool allowlist does not translate: the Codex sandbox and approval policy govern each
agent.

