<!-- IF:LIGHT_TASKS -->
## Work is tracked as light tasks

This project keeps its task list in the project itself, one file per task under `tasks/`, and not
in GitHub issues (`tasks.default` is `light` in `{{CONFIG_REL}}`). Review is still a pull request.

| Step | Command | What it does |
| ---- | ------- | ------------ |
| 1. See what is next | `cckit next` · `cckit task list` | The task to take, and every open task with its state |
| 2. Add work | `cckit task new --kind <post\|campaign\|brand\|research> "<title>"` | Records a task; nothing is shared yet |
| 3. Start | `cckit task start <id>` | A separate folder and branch for this task; work there |
| 4. Send for review | `cckit task finish <id> "<summary>" --all` | Opens the pull request; report the link and stop |

`--all` includes the files created for the task. Without it `finish` sends only files that already
existed and lists the new ones it left out, so a new draft would not reach the reviewer.

Create a GitHub issue only when {{OWNER_NAME}} asks for one.
<!-- /IF:LIGHT_TASKS -->

